a run aborted by a non-StandardError
  drains the nesting stack either way
  an exception that indicates a fault in the action (SystemStackError, ScriptError, …)
    settles into an exception-outcome result that .call returns rather than raising
    still raises through call!, as the original object
    reports it once, so a runaway recursion is no longer invisible to error tracking
    fires on_error alongside on_exception (the documented superset), and neither on_failure nor the success path
    records an honest exception outcome rather than leaving the run reading as a success
    logs the completion line at the exception outcome, not as a success
    covers the whole ScriptError family, not just SystemStackError
    settles the same way when raised from a before hook
    settles the same way when raised from an around hook
    settles the same way when raised from a preprocess: callable
    settles the same way when raised from an exposes default: callable
    surfaces a runaway model: finder as the real exception rather than a blank-field violation
    still applies outbound defaults, so the returned result reads like any other failed one
    does not escape .call when a default: callable blows the stack while settling
    when the action declares fails_on for it
      reclassifies to a failure outcome, firing on_failure and skipping the report
      honors a broad `fails_on Exception` for the classes axn absorbs
    when a callback itself raises a non-StandardError
      keeps the action's own exception and still returns a result
      still propagates one axn never absorbs
    when an if:/unless: matcher callable raises
      treats a non-StandardError exactly like an ordinary one: warned, and simply not matching
      never turns a successful action into a failed one
    when nested
      reports once, at the innermost action, with the call chain
  an exception that axn must not interfere with
    covers Sidekiq's shutdown signal, which subclasses Interrupt
    covers a library's own private control-flow signal
    covers ActiveSupport::ErrorReporter::UnexpectedError
    leaves an enclosing Timeout.timeout able to convert its own signal
    Interrupt
      escapes with no report and no callbacks
      logs that it started but never that it completed
    SystemExit
      escapes with no report and no callbacks
      logs that it started but never that it completed
    Timeout::ExitException
      escapes with no report and no callbacks
      logs that it started but never that it completed
    NoMemoryError
      escapes with no report and no callbacks
      logs that it started but never that it completed

Axn::Async with ActiveJob adapter
  behaves like an async adapter interface
    async :active_job configuration
      includes the Axn::Async::Adapters::ActiveJob adapter module
      provides call_async class method
    integration with Axn actions
      provides call_async method on the class
    error handling
      raises LoadError when active_job is not available
  behaves like async adapter exception handling
    exception handling
      returns result on success
      does not raise on Axn::Failure (business logic failure)
      re-raises unexpected exceptions for retry
  behaves like async adapter per-class exception reporting
    per-class async_exception_reporting override
      when action has per-class override :only_exhausted
        does not trigger on_exception on intermediate attempts (respects per-class override)
      when action has per-class override :every_attempt
        triggers on_exception on every attempt (respects per-class override)
      when action has no per-class override
        falls back to global config behavior
  .call_async
    calls perform_later on the proxy class with context
    with delayed execution
      calls set(wait:) and perform_later when _async contains wait option
      calls set(wait_until:) and perform_later when _async contains wait_until option
      calls perform_later when _async is not a hash
      calls perform_later when _async is an empty hash
  ActiveJob-specific behavior
