Axn
  return shape
    when successful
      is ok
    when fail! (user facing error)
      is not ok
    when exception raised
      is not ok
  modifying exposed objects
    modifying exposed object
      returns the modified object
    modifying expected and re-exposed object
      returns the modified object AND MODIFIES THE OBJECT THAT WAS
    re-exposing an expected kwarg without a manual expose call
      exposes the mutated object without requiring an explicit expose call
  exposures on non-success paths
    when fail! is called
      auto-copies the expected kwarg to the result (fail!)
      preserves in-place mutations made before the failure (fail!)
      is not ok
    when an unhandled exception is raised
      auto-copies the expected kwarg to the result (exception)
      preserves in-place mutations made before the failure (exception)
      is not ok
    when an explicitly exposed field was set before fail!
      keeps the explicitly exposed value
      also auto-copies the expected kwarg

